# interplay_memlive_held_intermediate_depth2: An exec whose command buffer is at VA page 4099 waits on the gate (a barrier on child FIFO 1's next stamp) while the guest swaps a subtree: at depth 2 the root table's entry 1 (the last-level table of VA pages 4096-8191), at depth 3 the root table's entry 0 (the whole second-level table, VA pages 0-16M, the object list and every command buffer among them), each for a copy whose leaves for A, B and page 4099 name other pages. The FIFO copied the exec's payload before its barrier but reads its command buffer and makes its objects only when released: it runs the copy's command buffer, A (read before the hold) keeps its old page, and B is made over the copy's leaf.
